.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt CALTOOL-INIT 1
.Os 
.Sh NAME
.Nm caltool-init
.Nd initialize a Swift package containing an executable product
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm caltool init
[-hcm]
.Eo \&[  Fl d Ar directory Ec ]
.Eo \&[  Fl n Ar product Ec ]
.Fl t Ar template
.Nm caltool init
.Fl -generate-manpage
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The 
.Nm caltool-init No  utility initializes a package containing an executable product based on a given 
.Ar template Ns .
Some templates also have variants with fewer example parameters.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl c, Fl -with-completion
Add zsh and fish completion generation support to the executable product.
Does not apply to the "opaque" template.
.It Fl d, Fl -directory Ar directory
The directory containing the new package (default: the current directory). If the 
.Ar directory No  is specified and does not exist, it will be created.
.It Fl -generate-manpage
Generate the mdoc source for this manual page and write it to standard output.
.It Fl h, Fl -help
Show a help screen.
.It Fl m, Fl -with-more
Use a template variant with more example parameters. Applies only to
"basic" and "testing".
.It Fl n, Fl -name Ar product
The name of the product. If not specified, the name defaults to the kebab-case
form of the package name..
.It Fl t, Fl -template Ar template
The template to use.
.El
.Pp
The package name defaults to the last component of the specified directory path.
.Sh TEMPLATES
Templates provide starting points for different executable product configurations.
All generated products can generate help screens 
except those based on the "opaque" template. Only products based on the "manpage" template 
can generate manual pages.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Sy opaque
A product without help screen generation.
.It Sy basic
A product with a basic help screen.
.It Sy testing
A product with unit testing.
.It Sy manpage
A product with manual page generation.
.It Sy simple-tree
A product with commands and subcommands.
.It Sy stateful-tree
A product with stateful commands and subcommands.
.El
.Pp
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility returns zero on success and non-zero on failure.
.Pp
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr caltool 1 ,
.Xr caltool-install 1 ,
.Xr caltool-uninstall 1
.Pp
